    "result": "Perfect! \u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files.\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed the two failing tests in the frai-core suite:\n\n1. **Governance schema violation test** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`): Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `src/finetune/index.js`. The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n2. **Evaluation harness test** (`src/eval/index.test.js`): Fixed the `toxicityMetric` function signature in `src/eval/metrics.js` to accept `(outputs, references)` instead of `(outputs, bannedTerms)`. The issue was that `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but toxicityMetric was treating the references array as banned terms, causing all outputs to be flagged as toxic.\n\nAll public exports remain intact and backward-compatible.",
